From: GitHub Copilot <copilot@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: build chromaprint with bundled kissfft

chromaprint 1.6.0 auto-selects FFmpeg's libavutil av_tx FFT backend when
FFmpeg is present. Linking the static libavutil into VLC's shared
stream_out_chromaprint plugin fails on x86_64 because tx_float.o emits a
non-PIC relocation (R_X86_64_PC32 against ff_tx_tab_32_float) that cannot be
used in a shared object, and ffmpeg's --enable-pic does not make that object
position-independent.

Force the bundled KissFFT backend (vendored at src/3rdparty/kissfft) so the
plugin computes its FFT without linking libavutil at all. The fingerprint
output is unchanged.
---
 contrib/src/chromaprint/rules.mak | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/contrib/src/chromaprint/rules.mak b/contrib/src/chromaprint/rules.mak
--- a/contrib/src/chromaprint/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/chromaprint/rules.mak
@@ -27,5 +27,5 @@
 .chromaprint: chromaprint toolchain.cmake
 	$(CMAKECLEAN)
-	$(HOSTVARS_CMAKE) $(CMAKE) -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF
+	$(HOSTVARS_CMAKE) $(CMAKE) -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF -DFFT_LIB=kissfft -DKISSFFT_SOURCE_DIR=$(abspath $<)/src/3rdparty/kissfft
 	+$(CMAKEBUILD)
 	$(CMAKEINSTALL)
